{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057553-mechanical-effects-of-mage-sight","id":1057553,"title":"Mechanical Effects of Mage Sight","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-03T05:53:32-08:00","id":1057553,"title":"Mechanical Effects of Mage Sight","content":"I don't really understand mechanical effects of Mage Sight. For example, does mage with Active Mind Sight automatically notices all thinking creatures, no matter their Stealth? How do mundane efforts to conceal something work against Mage Sight?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T06:19:17-08:00","id":1057564,"title":"","content":"The thing you're looking at has to be in sensory range, so it would depend on if they're actually out of sight, hearing, etc. or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T10:42:18-08:00","id":1057652,"title":"","content":"The second paragraph of the Active Sight section states that the character must perceive the phenomenon in question. It can't be behind a wall or in another plane.<br /> <br /> A Mage with Active Mind Sight wouldn't sense a person hiding in a tree, but if the tree itself is sapient, they'd know it. They wouldn't hear someone moving perfectly silently, but if they heard a mysterious droning, they would know it was being made by something intelligent (even if they don't know it's a swarm of sapient robo-bees).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T15:59:59-08:00","id":1057795,"title":"","content":"What if they had a spell on them giving them, say, ability to perceive things through gravity (&quot;gravity sense&quot;) or a spell that gives them ability to sense minds (&quot;mind sight&quot;)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T16:29:48-08:00","id":1057818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057553-mechanical-effects-of-mage-sight?p=1057795#post1057795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if they had a spell on them giving them, say, ability to perceive things through gravity (&amp;quot;gravity sense&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> or a spell that gives them ability to sense minds (&amp;quot;mind sight&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />?</div> </div> </div> </div>While I dunno if there's a rule addressing this, my gut feeling is to allow Unveiling or similar enhancement spells to stack with Mage Sight. <br /> <br /> For example, Outward and Inward Eye could get rid of &quot;you can't see through walls and doors&quot; restriction, and Zoom In could be used to scan with Mage Sight from miles away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T16:40:57-08:00","id":1057828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057553-mechanical-effects-of-mage-sight?p=1057795#post1057795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if they had a spell on them giving them, say, ability to perceive things through gravity (&quot;gravity sense&quot;) or a spell that gives them ability to sense minds (&quot;mind sight&quot;)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm constantly using Mage Sight through The Outward and Inward Eye (once supplemented with Zoom and Heightened Senses to look over a whole neighborhood). To me it was always clear that if you have your senses enhanced it would also enhance your Mage Sight. Was that asumption wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T17:24:05-08:00","id":1057848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057553-mechanical-effects-of-mage-sight?p=1057652#post1057652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second paragraph of the Active Sight section states that the character must perceive the phenomenon in question. It can't be behind a wall or in another plane.<br /> <br /> A Mage with Active Mind Sight wouldn't sense a person hiding in a tree, but if the tree itself is sapient, they'd know it. They wouldn't hear someone moving perfectly silently, but if they heard a mysterious droning, they would know it was being made by something intelligent (even if they don't know it's a swarm of sapient robo-bees).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So you can't hear the thoughts of a person hiding behind a sofa in the same room as you? I thought Active Mind Sight would pick up on the static of thought processes, like a mind signature or beacon alerting you that a thinking being is near. Then you could use other methods to decipher what that thinking being is contemplating.<br /> <br /> Does it make a difference if they're hiding inside of a tree or lurking around the corner? Presumably, a lurker around the corner is still within sensory range if noise would give them away.<br /> <br /> Or do we only count it if they're actively communicating information via that sensory path? Meaning you can cast a spell on someone you can hear for as long as you can hear them, then once they go silent, you lose their signal. Same as losing their scent or losing sight of them.<br /> <br /> Put another way, you could conceivable use Active Mind Sight on them if they either made themselves visible to your eyes, or audible? Does that also mean you could use their smell to detect their thoughts? Familiar perfume? Or maybe a life or matter spell to detect a certain pheromone or substance? ... Does that mean you could detect them in the room with Active Mind Sight if you were chewing on a lock of their hair or licking an amputated finger? lol<br /> <br /> EDIT: I assume the last bit would translate into sympathy magic unless you were tasting their physical person, at which point you've found your target without needing to use Mind Sight ... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":11166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","user":"kryptonitekrusher","date":". 03-03-2017, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T19:21:18-08:00","id":1057880,"title":"","content":"If you can receive sensory information (Any sensory information) of their presence or a live feed you can perceive them with Mage Sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T19:48:40-08:00","id":1057894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057553-mechanical-effects-of-mage-sight?p=1057880#post1057880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you can receive sensory information (Any sensory information) of their presence or a live feed you can perceive them with Mage Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My issue with this is, in the example above the person is hiding in a tree. How much concealment does the tree provide? If you were to speak in a hallowed out tree and I can hear you as I walk past, does that mean I can pick up your mind with Active Mind Sight?<br /> <br /> I'm wondering if Mind Sight checks the physical space and verifies if a wall is too thick, another way to think of it is whether or not it is dampened by the nature of the material between you and your target. A water resistant tent versus a one-foot thick reinforced titanium door.<br /> <br /> If it works how you explained, then it operates on the presumption of <i>can</i> (as in not presently happening, but possible to occur.) Meaning the person within the tree is not 100% hidden unless it is deemed that the tree provides enough concealment to hide the person from mundane senses. Like thoughts that would have been audible are sufficiently dampened by the tree, versus the guy in the shadows has nothing to dampen his thoughts and is clearly heard despite skulking quietly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T20:00:52-08:00","id":1057902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057553-mechanical-effects-of-mage-sight?p=1057894#post1057894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it works how you explained, then it operates on the presumption of <i>can</i> (as in not presently happening, but possible to occur.) Meaning the person within the tree is not 100% hidden unless it is deemed that the tree provides enough concealment to hide the person from mundane senses. Like thoughts that would have been audible are sufficiently dampened by the tree, versus the guy in the shadows has nothing to dampen his thoughts and is clearly heard despite skulking quietly.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you couldn't perceive the person in the tree with your mundane senses then you couldn't perceive him with Mind Sight, the same goes for the guy skulking in the shadows. Mage Sight offers some enhancements to your mundane perceptions but they work in a lateral direction rather than a progressive one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T20:20:27-08:00","id":1057911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057553-mechanical-effects-of-mage-sight?p=1057902#post1057902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you couldn't perceive the person in the tree with your mundane senses then you couldn't perceive him with Mind Sight, the same goes for the guy skulking in the shadows. Mage Sight offers some enhancements to your mundane perceptions but they work in a lateral direction rather than a progressive one.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I can't hear the skulker's thoughts unless I actually see him or he makes a noise? I especially thought that Active Mage Sight could, because I could've sworn that Active Death Sight could see even in-active ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T20:24:07-08:00","id":1057912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057553-mechanical-effects-of-mage-sight?p=1057911#post1057911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I can't hear the skulker's thoughts unless I actually see him or he makes a noise? I especially thought that Active Mage Sight could, because I could've sworn that Active Death Sight could see even in-active ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That only comes with the Death 2 Utility Attainment that specifically upgrades that part of your Mage Sight which comes along with inactive ghosts pinging PMS. The Mind 2 Utility Attainment specifically only allows you to detect goetia lingering in Twilight so it still wouldn't be able to detect the skulker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T07:16:53-08:00","id":1058030,"title":"","content":"You actually can't hear a person's thoughts with Mind Sight; you can simply tell if the thing you're looking at is able to think. It's not like the thing suddenly becomes brighter or more obvious; more like it suddenly gets painted a new colour that instantly tells you something when you see it. If you can't see the thing, you can't see the colour.<br /> <br /> Worth noting that Active Mage Sight actively makes it <i>harder</i> to detect stuff as well (that -2 to actions Active Mage Sight inflicts <i>includes</i> sensory perception). The Mage is tripping balls; their vision and senses just got <i>more</i> cluttered. It's like suddenly having the infrared and ultraviolet+ spectra of light overlaid suddenly on your vision; you can definitely tell new information from it, but it's all there at once and overwhelming enough that only looking for looking for specific details can possibly make it clear.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T20:00:09-08:00","id":1058268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057553-mechanical-effects-of-mage-sight?p=1058030#post1058030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You actually can't hear a person's thoughts with Mind Sight; you can simply tell if the thing you're looking at is able to think. It's not like the thing suddenly becomes brighter or more obvious; more like it suddenly gets painted a new colour that instantly tells you something when you see it. If you can't see the thing, you can't see the colour.<br /> <br /> Worth noting that Active Mage Sight actively makes it <i>harder</i> to detect stuff as well (that -2 to actions Active Mage Sight inflicts <i>includes</i> sensory perception). The Mage is tripping balls; their vision and senses just got <i>more</i> cluttered. It's like suddenly having the infrared and ultraviolet+ spectra of light overlaid suddenly on your vision; you can definitely tell new information from it, but it's all there at once and overwhelming enough that only looking for looking for specific details can possibly make it clear.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That makes a ton more sense--the assigning of details to what is already observed.<br /> <br /> Then how would you hear the droning of a swarm if you can't see them? Is it because you're using Active Mind Sight on noise you can already hear, and then AMS lets you know there are thousands of unique minds in that source?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T20:22:33-08:00","id":1058276,"title":"","content":"Active Mage Sight is interpretation of information drawn through all your senses. There's no reason it would only apply to sight, despite what the name might imply; humans are simply more sight dependent, so we get proportionately less information through our other senses. A Thyrsus who, say, uses Heightened Senses, though, could probably sniff out toxins in someone's blood from across a pitch black room with Life Sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T21:49:15-08:00","id":1058292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057553-mechanical-effects-of-mage-sight?p=1058276#post1058276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Active Mage Sight is interpretation of information drawn through all your senses. There's no reason it would only apply to sight, despite what the name might imply; humans are simply more sight dependent, so we get proportionately less information through our other senses. A Thyrsus who, say, uses Heightened Senses, though, could probably sniff out toxins in someone's blood from across a pitch black room with Life Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So AMS is not x-ray vision or infrared goggles.<br /> <br /> If a stimulus occurs or is presently occurring and it utilizes one of the five senses, if your AMS is active, it will ping on info relevant to that particular AMS arcana being used.<br /> <br /> With Life Sight, are you able to identify those specific toxins? Or are you seeing that the body is behaving like a one does when toxins are introduced? I ask because I assume toxicology falls under Matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T04:28:12-08:00","id":1058358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kryptonitekrusher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057553-mechanical-effects-of-mage-sight?p=1058292#post1058292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So AMS is not x-ray vision or infrared goggles.<br /> <br /> If a stimulus occurs or is presently occurring and it utilizes one of the five senses, if your AMS is active, it will ping on info relevant to that particular AMS arcana being used.<br /> <br /> With Life Sight, are you able to identify those specific toxins? Or are you seeing that the body is behaving like a one does when toxins are introduced? I ask because I assume toxicology falls under Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously.<br /> <br /> Life Sight says it detects the presence of toxins, not what they are. If it did it would say so. You'd require spells to get more specific, and/or FMS if it was supernatural in origin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T08:09:55-08:00","id":1058410,"title":"","content":"Life Sight lets you identify the disruption that a specific toxin is causing to the body and that a toxin is present, yes. Any further details are a matter for other spells - Life or Matter, depending on their nature - to discern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T09:29:16-08:00","id":1058446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057553-mechanical-effects-of-mage-sight?p=1058410#post1058410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life Sight lets you identify the disruption that a specific toxin is causing to the body and that a toxin is present, yes. Any further details are a matter for other spells - Life or Matter, depending on their nature - to discern.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for helping me get that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T12:27:55-08:00","id":1058516,"title":"","content":"No problem, muchacho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:02:40-08:00","id":1058529,"title":"","content":"As another posted mentioned, the Mage Sight spoilers from Signs of Sorcery are very helpful.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9YzBRVWpGYzNFZ0U/view\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0Bxv...pGYzNFZ0U/view</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Per the spoiler, each Arcanum's Active Mage Sight provides certain mechanical advantages:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Each Arcanum has a minor mechanical effect, relating to the base level of perception granted by Active Sight.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Death</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Sight allows a mage to detect the presence of the Anchor Condition (p. XX) or manifested ghosts and related phenomena. With a glance, a mage using Mage Sight can tell if someone has a soul, or if a body is, in fact, dead.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Fate</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Sight highlights anyone the mage watches who experiences a dramatic failure or exceptional success. It reveals the presence and use of a Destiny (see Merits, p. XX), but not the details of that destiny.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Forces</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Sight detects motion and highlights the presence of environmental Tilts, fire, electricity, and other hazards. With a glance, a mage can tell if a device is powered.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Life </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Sight detects life signs, revealing if a body is still alive, and allows a mage to gauge how injured a character is with a glance. The presence of toxins, diseases, and Personal Tilts is obvious to the mage.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Matter</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Sight allows the mage to determine the Structure and Durability of anything she looks at, as well as highlighting the value and quality of items (in game terms, telling the player the Availability and Equipment Bonus of any object).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Mind </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Sight detects the presence of thinking beings and allows the mage to tell with a glance if someone is asleep, comatose, awake, meditating, or projecting out of his body or into the Astral. The mage is also aware when a character she observes gains or spends Willpower.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Prime</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Sight highlights anything the mage can use as a Yantra, and the presence (if not the composition) of any Awakened spell or Attainment effect. Mages using Prime Sight can recognize tass with a glance, and tell when they are in a Hallow or Node.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Space</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Sight allows the user to instantly judge distances, range bands, and cover, allowing the player to know what bonuses or penalties would be in effect before the character acts. It also detects spatial warps, scrying windows, and the presence of Irises.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Spirit </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Sight reveals the strength of the local Gauntlet, detects the presence and nature of the Resonance Condition and other sources of Essence, and highlights manifested spirits and related phenomena.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Time</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"> Sight reveals the split-second adjustments of time, allowing the player to know the Initiative ratings of all participants in combat. When a character is about to act, even with a reflexive action, a mage watching with Time Sight is aware of it (if not what that action will be), and may preempt it if he is able. Time Sight also detects temporal warps, and the tell-tale signs that someone has come back into the past.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T13:21:13-08:00","id":1058538,"title":"","content":"That's not the Signs of Sorcery spoiler; that's all in the Mage 2e core. It got spoiled pre-release so that the Signs spoiler was legible to people who didn't have the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T14:14:15-08:00","id":1058565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057553-mechanical-effects-of-mage-sight?p=1058538#post1058538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not the Signs of Sorcery spoiler; that's all in the Mage 2e core. It got spoiled pre-release so that the Signs spoiler was legible to people who didn't have the book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Indeed! It's been awhile since I read that section of the core, and got confused with the SoS spoilers.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I imagine that SoS will then provide even more juicy Mage Sight mechanics and benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T14:18:25-08:00","id":1058567,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0BxveHUKxwBU9ejlGcDYtN3hZTWs/view\" target=\"_blank\">They definitely seem to.</a> The Keen Periphery and Piercing Glance merits seem like must-haves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:17:18-08:00","id":1058602,"title":"","content":"I forgot how amazing these two would be on a Prime Detective. These two plus Mana Sensitivity make you a great investigator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T10:53:24-08:00","id":1060174,"title":"","content":"Okay, one more question about MS: does Peripheral Mage Sight reacts just to things which are in the radius of normal sense, or it reacts to everything supernaturally active nearby? How far does it detect in this case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T11:08:33-08:00","id":1060184,"title":"","content":"A Prime based investigator uncovering the Truth with a capital T used to be cool, and now is super super cool, mechanically and conceptually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-08T11:43:18-08:00","id":1060196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057553-mechanical-effects-of-mage-sight?p=1060174#post1060174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, one more question about MS: does Peripheral Mage Sight reacts just to things which are in the radius of normal sense, or it reacts to everything supernaturally active nearby? How far does it detect in this case?</div> </div> </div> </div>It reacts to all active supernatural effects going on inside the range of your normal senses that aren't designed to go unnoticed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T10:42:33-08:00","id":1060930,"title":"","content":"God, I can't understand the following paragraph at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Concealment magic, of whatever type, can hide a target from Active Mage Sight, but only if the concealment would logically mask the target from the purview of the Arcanum in question. Even then, if the concealment power uses the same magical principles as the detecting Arcanum, the mage still has a chance to see through it. For example, a light-based invisibility spell would conceal a target from Mind Sight, but Life Sight could still detect the living being, with or without the assistance of photons. </div> </div> </div>What does &quot;logically mask the target from the purview of the Arcanum in question&quot; means? The example in question isn't logical at all: if Life Sight can sense the presence of living being by sensing it's Life, why can't the Mind Sight sense the presence of thinking being by by sensing it's Mind? Or does this spell block any type of Sight anything except Force Sight? Why then Life Sight is included? How would be Mind Sight different from theoretical spell &quot;Sense Mind&quot;, which would give mage information of living beings around, and how would it interact with not-so-theoretical spell &quot;Invisibility&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T10:57:05-08:00","id":1060938,"title":"","content":"I have to admit, that paragraph is pretty confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T11:22:40-08:00","id":1060950,"title":"","content":"Since the paragraph isn't logical it must be assumed that it was a typo and they didn't mean Mind they meant Forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T11:48:33-08:00","id":1060962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1057553-mechanical-effects-of-mage-sight?p=1060950#post1060950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the paragraph isn't logical it must be assumed that it was a typo and they didn't mean Mind they meant Forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I have thought too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T13:27:16-08:00","id":1061324,"title":"","content":"Okay, now after I read this on more time, I've lost the track of meaning of author's thought completely. Help me out, please?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For example, a light-based invisibility spell would conceal a target from <b>Force </b>Sight, but Life Sight could still detect the living being, with or without the assistance of photons. </div> </div> </div>Here, if we replace &quot;Mind&quot; with &quot;Force&quot;, the suggestion seems to be that Veiling Practice in Arcanum protects only from Arcanum Sight. So, <b>if </b>subject invisible, you <b>can't </b>detect bending of photons, but you still <b>can </b>feel his life, sense his thoughts, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Likewise, some vampires employ a kind of mental \u201cinvisibility\u201d that causes observers to ignore them. This power would conceal a target from Forces Sight (it isn\u2019t light-based) or Time Sight, but not Mind Sight (since both the concealment power and the Arcanum are working on the same principles). </div> </div> </div>And here, the meaning is completely reversed: the suggestion seems to be that Veiling Practice in Arcanum <b>does not</b> protects only from Arcanum Sight - every other Arcanum Sight is blocked! So, <b>if </b>subject invisible, you <b>can </b>detect bending of photons, but <b>can't </b>feel his life, sense his thoughts, etc.<br /> <br /> Which reading is correct? Both are kind of logical in their own way, but second makes Veiling much more powerful - for example, nobody but other Forces user can detect invisible mage, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","user":"Dark Archon","date":". 03-11-2017, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T13:43:57-08:00","id":1061328,"title":"","content":"Someone somewhere someday unpacked this section and I think there was some sensible conclusion to it. I don't remember where or when. I think it involved Mrmdubois, as usual when good things are said. I remember this specific issue being deciphered or close to deciphered...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T14:23:02-08:00","id":1061336,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11880_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11880\" data-vbnamecard=\"11880\">Dark Archon</a> I think Active Mage Sight entitles you to a CoW against an effect that would fall under the purview of the arcana that the Mage is using for his AMS. Some forms of Veiling bypass the CoW entirely though, so AMS Life bypasses your Forces invisibility by picking up on the signals that Life can find since you as a person are made up of more than just light bending or reflecting around your body to conceal it. You can't see the invisible person because Life doesn't care about photons, but you can know a living body is there (From our earlier discussions I would say that the person hiding with Forces would have to be giving off sensory information that your Life Sight could work with, scent or hearing for instance). If you used Forces you could get a CoW and if you win you'd be rewarded with bypassing their Veiling effect altogether, in other words you could see the invisible person, the illusion no longer affects you. Some Veiling effects can only be perceived after they lose out in a CoW, the vampire effect or Incognito for instance &quot;edit&quot; your brain's memories or processes to ignore the thing you're looking at so even if you can see them with Forces or Life or whatever you'll just ignore the information because of the mental effect. A lot of Veiling effects have this setup, for instance it doesn't matter how strong your Forces sight is you won't be able to detect a Fate Veiling effect without using Fate AMS, and then you can't pierce the effect without wining in a CoW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}